{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>ההולכת למואל</b> — those who go to their side and opposite them. The alef in the word למואל is in place of the vav of ממולי, and the vav is for extension. Similar to it: אם לא יגיד ונשא עונו, in which the vav is for extension." "<b>להחומה</b> — with the definite article, as is proper."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The cited phrase אם לא יגיד ונשא עונו (Leviticus 5:1) retains the vav prefix; Ibn Ezra's point is that the vav extends the conditional force to the second verb. Left untranslated as Hebrew script per discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:39.356470552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}